tether (`tether/`), the pseudo-terminal host the daemon runs sessions in, is a project of its
own under the same licence, with its own NOTICE in `tether/NOTICE`.

No speech engine is part of this distribution: not sherpa-onnx, the runtime they run on (its
native library carries espeak-ng, GPL-3.0), nor the Moonshine, Whisper, Nemotron, Piper,
Kokoro or Supertonic models. A node downloads one from where its makers publish it only when its user asks, after
the app has shown the licences it comes under, and it is then the user's under those
licences.

